# W3b completion record

Date: 2026-07-20
Branch: `feat/forms-runner`

## Required findings

- R1 resolved. Successful `/raw` and `/embed` artifact-HTML responses set the exact CSP `sandbox allow-scripts allow-forms allow-popups`; neither includes `allow-same-origin`. The `/view` HTML iframe uses the exact attribute `sandbox="allow-scripts allow-forms allow-popups"`, also without `allow-same-origin`. The response headers are applied in `server.js` even when forms are disabled, so the artifact boundary protects other first-party mutations too. `/asset` serves `.html`/`.htm` as `text/plain`, `/view` either sanitizes authored HTML or frames `/embed`, published HTML readback reaches the same sandboxed `/raw` helper, and the virtual published repository has no executable `/embed` readback.
- R2 resolved in code. `test/forms-runner.test.js` contains a Google Chrome headless canary that serves authored script, attempts credentialed form fetch/token extraction/submission, covers direct `/embed` and `/view` framing, and asserts that no record is written. Direct `/embed` makes removal of its CSP observable as a durable-write failure; `/view` also has the independent iframe sandbox. This execution sandbox prohibits loopback listeners (`listen EPERM`), so the browser canary reported one explicit skip here; it runs normally and fails closed in an environment that permits local listeners.
- R3 resolved. Origin validation has no `Host`/`req.protocol` fallback. Missing or wholly invalid configured origins produce a startup warning and browser mutations fail closed. YAML supports explicit `forms.publicOrigins` lists; both Origin and Referer must match the same configured exact scheme/host/port. Express proxy trust defaults to false, and cookie `Secure` derives only from explicit configured origins. A hostile matching Host regression writes no record.
- R4 resolved. Store `EVALIDATION` becomes HTTP 400, idempotency `ECONFLICT` becomes HTTP 409, schema validation remains HTTP 422, and route-scoped parser size errors become HTTP 413. Error responses are bounded messages. The terminal error logger records only error name/code, never stacks, messages, absolute paths, or filesystem objects. Tests cover malformed timestamp, bad timezone, offset mismatch, fractional offset, idempotency conflict, oversized JSON, and response/log path redaction.
- R5 resolved. Form render, submit, receipt-read, and denial events use an allowlisted event shape and the existing API-key audit primitive when configured; local Operator/no-store deployments use the same redacted event through the structured logger fallback. Outcomes include accepted, rejected authentication/authorization/origin/CSRF/validation/size/idempotency. Audit tests prove CSRF material, values, labels, option labels, and filesystem paths are absent.
- R6 resolved. Every captured value now requires and persists server-derived `fieldLabel` next to `fieldType`; receipt rendering prefers this snapshot. A receipt issued before a template label rename continues to render the original label. Client-supplied metadata/labels remain rejected.

## Advisories

- A1 applied: validation re-render calls the safe context issuer, so an eviction race rotates to a fresh context instead of dereferencing `undefined`; regression covered.
- A2 deferred: TTL/login/logout rotation requires a real authenticated browser-session lifecycle; v1 still has only ambient local Operator contexts.
- A3 applied: exact configured origin lists are supported and documented in `lookie-link.yaml.example`.
- A4 partially applied: oversized JSON is 413 and parser/credential denials are audited; authentication/envelope ordering remains the binding ADR-92 ordering rather than changing concealment semantics in this patch.
- A5 deferred: the shared forms capability service is external work; restricted mode continues to fail closed.
- A6 applied: untrusted forwarded protocol cannot set `Secure` or define the accepted origin; proxy trust defaults off and cookie security follows explicit origin configuration.
- A7 deferred: registry caching and the template-version TOCTOU require a pinned form/version model, beyond a cheap route fix.
- A8 deferred: descriptor-relative/no-follow filesystem work is a separate local-filesystem hardening change; the current registry still rejects observed symlinks and remains non-recursive.
- A9 deferred: idempotency indexing is a scaling projection change; correctness and immutable replay remain covered.
- A10 deferred: routing a private list API expands the requested forms-runner surface and is not needed for the create/submit/restart/receipt exit gate.

## Previously-sound properties reverified

- CSRF exact-origin/Referer and synchronizer-token checks still reject missing, wrong, cross-origin, and query-token submissions without records.
- Receipt authorization still conceals a submission from a different principal and permits an explicitly authorized submissions reader.
- Template/submission traversal remains uniform 404 without filesystem disclosure; registry last-known-good behavior still passes.
- Client-forged actor, submission ID, receipt timestamp, option label, and capture-label attempts are rejected without records.
- Form, receipt, captured label, option label, and submitted value HTML remains escaped.
- Record publication remains mode 0600, has one final link after publication, cannot overwrite an existing ID, and idempotent replay remains immutable.
- Forms routes remain absent unless `forms.enabled === true`.

